.TH SOOKIE 1 "November 2026" "Sookie 51.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sookie \- Wayland compositor and window manager for the Cali desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sookie
[\fIOPTION\fR...] [[\-\-] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENT\fR...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBsookie\fR is a Wayland display server and window manager, based on GNOME's
Mutter. It is the compositor behind the Cali desktop environment (CaliDE).
X11 applications are supported through Xwayland.
.PP
Running \fBsookie\fR directly starts it with the default plugin. This is meant
for development and debugging; a full desktop session runs Sookie through
\fBcali-compositor\fR.
.PP
If \fICOMMAND\fR is given, it is started inside the session once the compositor
is ready.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-wayland
Run as a Wayland compositor.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-x11
Run the Wayland compositor without starting Xwayland.
.TP
.BI \-\-wayland\-display= NAME
Use \fINAME\fR as the Wayland display name.
.TP
.B \-\-display\-server
Run as a full display server on the hardware, rather than nested.
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run as a headless display server.
.TP
.BI \-\-virtual\-monitor= WxH[@R]
Add a persistent virtual monitor, for example \fB1920x1080@60\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-devkit
Show the session in a window using the development kit.
.TP
.BI \-\-devkit\-args= ARGS
Extra arguments passed to the development kit.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile= FILE
Record a performance trace to \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-control
Enable the debug control D-Bus interface.
.TP
.BI \-\-mutter\-plugin= PLUGIN
Load \fIPLUGIN\fR instead of the default plugin. The option keeps its upstream
name for compatibility.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-?, \-\-help
Show a summary of options.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a nested session in a window and start a text editor inside it:
.PP
.RS
.B dbus-run-session sookie \-\-wayland \-\-devkit \-\- gnome-text-editor
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are stored in GSettings under the \fIorg.gnome.mutter\fR schemas,
which Sookie shares with Mutter for compatibility with GNOME tools.
